    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "INTEGER MATH\n\nAdd, Subtract, Multiply, Divide and Modulo work on whole numbers (i64).\nInteger divide drops the remainder (7 / 3 = 2) and Modulo returns it (7 % 3 = 1).\nEach result is written to a variable so you can inspect it in the debugger.\nBitwise nodes treat the number as bits: 12 = 0b1100, 10 = 0b1010.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          190.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "HOW TO READ THE GRAPH\nBegin Play runs nine Set nodes in a row. Each Set takes its value from the math node wired into it (a and b are typed on the node as literals). Expected: sum 10, difference 4, product 21, quotient 2, remainder 1, AND 8, OR 14, XOR 6, 1 << 4 = 16.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -70.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
